<article>
    <topic>
        <title>Precedences</title>
        <p>
            Precedences of all kinds of expressions are listed below in descending precedence.
            Parentheses group an expression: <b>(EXPRESSION)</b> can be used wherever a precedence-1 expression is required.
            For example, <b>(1 + 2) * 3</b> evaluates the addition first.
        </p>
        <topic>
            <title>1</title>
            <p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Literals, names and other primitive expressions.</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b>.observe ( ... )</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b>.observe as NAME ( ... )</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b>( ... )</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b>.NAME</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b>::NAME</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b>[ ... ]</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b> in ...</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b> not in ...</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b> of TYPE</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b> as TYPE</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b> as *</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b> is TYPE</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b> is not TYPE</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b> is null</li>
                    <li><b>&lt;EXPR-PRECEDENCE-1&gt;</b> is not null</li>
                </ul>
            </p>
            <p>
                The collection operand after <b>in</b> or <b>not in</b> is a full expression.
                When combining a membership result with another operator, write <b>(value in values) and condition</b>
                or <b>(value not in values) and condition</b> to keep that operator outside the collection operand.
            </p>
        </topic>
        <topic>
            <title>2 (unary operators)</title>
            <p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>+</b></li>
                    <li><b>-</b></li>
                    <li><b>not</b></li>
                    <li><b>cast</b></li>
                    <li><b>variant in</b></li>
                </ul>
                These unary operators group from right to left.
                For example, <b>cast int variant in value</b> means <b>cast int (variant in value)</b>.
            </p>
        </topic>
        <topic>
            <title>3</title>
            <p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>^</b></li>
                </ul>
            </p>
        </topic>
